<% @page_description = "What Smartfire is: self-hosted, open-source team chat run by the organization hosting each workspace." %>

<h1>About Smartfire</h1>
<p class="public-lede">
  Smartfire is self-hosted, open-source team chat. Each workspace runs on its own
  server, operated by the organization that set it up, and that organization
  controls its workspace's data.
</p>

<h2>What you can do here</h2>
<ul>
  <li>Talk in rooms organized by topic or team, with threads for side conversations.</li>
  <li>Share files, both uploads stored on the workspace server and Google Drive links.</li>
  <li>Plan with room events, and optionally publish your Going and Maybe RSVPs to your own Google Calendar.</li>
  <li>Meet over voice and video huddles without leaving the room.</li>
  <li>Connect optional integrations your workspace enables, such as GitHub pull-request cards, bots, and agents.</li>
</ul>

<h2>Signing in with Google</h2>
<p>
  Where the workspace enables it, members can sign in with their Google Workspace
  account. Google sign-in only verifies your identity: it does not connect your
  calendar or your Drive files. Connecting Google Calendar or Drive previews is a
  separate, optional choice you make later from your profile.
</p>

<h2>Your data stays with this workspace</h2>
<p>
  Messages you post, including direct messages, and files you upload are stored on
  this workspace's server and may remain in its backups. People who operate that
  server can access that data. Room membership still controls what ordinary
  members can see. The
  <%= link_to "privacy policy", privacy_path %> explains this in detail; the
  <%= link_to "terms of service", terms_path %> covers the rules for using the workspace.
</p>

<% operator_name = PublicPolicy.operator_name %>
<% contact_email = PublicPolicy.contact_email %>
<% if operator_name || contact_email %>
  <h2>Who runs this workspace</h2>
  <% if operator_name %>
    <p>This workspace is operated by <strong><%= operator_name %></strong>.</p>
  <% end %>
  <% if contact_email %>
    <p>Contact: <%= mail_to contact_email %></p>
  <% end %>
<% end %>

<p><%= link_to "Sign in to this workspace", new_session_path %></p>
